From 343a3ee8a24f3daa3bbf211dbbcc67e0a5addc93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:44:15 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Per-provider retention: skip providers an article
 outlived

Pool::with_retention sets how long a provider keeps articles, and
BodyExpectation::posted (or stat_in_lane's posted) says when an article was
posted. Client routing skips a provider the article's age is past, as a miss it
does not remember, so a release no provider retains ends NotFound without a
request. Imports date every request by the NZB's newest file; a SegmentReader
or vfs::Reader takes the date with with_posted.
